{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71231-assorted-dtd-rules-questions","id":71231,"title":"Assorted DtD rules questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-13T06:39:32-08:00","id":71231,"title":"Assorted DtD rules questions","content":"I've mostly finished digesting the rules and am going to start a new campaign this weekend but wanted to clarify a number of general questions and unlikely-to-come-up corner case scenarios<br /> <br /> <u><b>Primum and Glitches</b></u><ul><li>Page 184 states that you can get permanent glitches when you lower your Primum and p 108 states that if your Primum decreases your permanent glitches become transient. How does that all work?... So Suppose I am at Primum 9 and increase to Primum 10. So I roll 3 for permanent Glitches and, say, I get 2 permanent Glitches. Then I somehow drop to 9. What happens? The way I read the combined effect of pages 184 and 108 is that the two permanent glitches become transient but then I roll for 2 permanent glitches because I dropped to 9. So I now actually have 4 Glitches - 2 transient and 2 permanent. Is that right?..</li> </ul><ul><li>If my analysis of Glitches above is correct then what happens when you Go Loud? You go up to 10 Primum, get some glitches. But because Going Loud is a temporary state, those glitches are transient (or become transient when you return to your normal Primum). And for Primum 1-5 there are no glitch rolls so we are good. So far that is consistent with the RAW. But do you roll for new glitches when you return from Primum 10 to your normal level of, say, Primum 6?</li> </ul><ul><li>Page 196 says you can swap two demonic forms whenever a new level of Primum is purchases. Is that specific to *purchasing* Primum or does it include increasing Primum via, say, unlocking an Interlock?</li> </ul><ul><li>Can Primum be decreases other than by prologued exposure to facilities?</li> </ul><ul><li>Are restoration facilities...erm, facilities? In the sense that are you risking losing Primum if you go there to remove your Glitches?</li> </ul><ul><li>Exceptional successes on the extended roll at the restoration facilities. The possible effects include (1) refilling your Aether pool, (2) reducing the time required for each roll, (3) subtracting the relevant skill from the target number. In addition, you should (4) get a positive condition. But the roll is Int+Sta+Prim. No skill. So what do you subtract for option (3)? Primum? And, as above, what sort of conditions might be appropriate? There aren't many demon-specific positive conditions. Inspired?...</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Compromise Rolls</u></b><ul><li>Cam Willpower be used to boost Compromise rolls? On the one hand you can use WP to prevent a roll from an Exploit but on the other hand you can't use WP on glitch rolls. And also I don't think you can use WP on breaking point rolls which are similar...</li> </ul><ul><li>Can Willpower be used to avoid compromise rolls from Embeds (in the rare cases when an Embed would cause a compromise roll)?</li> </ul><ul><li>What is the Cover penalty for rolling for compromise while in Demonic form? I don't mean a compromise roll cause by assuming the demonic form but an unrelated compromise while in the demonic form? Is it still -3?</li> </ul><ul><li>If you maintain a partial transformation for more than a scene, do you still get the cumulative -1 penalty on compromise rolls?</li> </ul><ul><li>What sort of Conditions are appropriate for getting an exceptional success on a compromise roll? I assume the general rule that exceptional successes give positive conditions still stands... Maybe Steadfast?..</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Miscellaneous</b></u><ul><li>Are there any Aether sources that can be detected without activating Aether Resonance? If you are at Aether 0 does that mean you can't even identify a possible source of Aether to replenish from?</li> </ul><ul><li>How do Demons learn Embeds and Exploits? I mean what sort of activities are required apart from expending XP? Do you need research into the relevant phenomenon? If you are friendly with a demon and he is willing to teach you what does that teaching involve? Is it instantaneous or do Demons have to put effort and time into acquiring new abilities?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:34:16-08:00","id":71273,"title":"","content":"The references to losing Primum are leftover from an earlier version of the rules, there is no way to lose Primum you have purchased or received from your Cipher. The glitches received from Going Loud would be temporary glitches that will last a lot longer than Going Loud lasts due to temporary glitches lasting a long time with 10 Primum. <br /> <br /> I don't think that Willpower can be spent on Compromise rolls. It can possibly be used to avoid compromises with Embeds, because some Embeds state that they cause Compromise on Success, but not on Exceptional Success. So you can't use it on the Compromise roll, but you can use it on the Embed roll to possibly avoid making a Compromise roll.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success on a Compromise roll says that it gives a Cover Beat or regular Beat and a point of Willpower, I don't think it should grant a positive condition as well considering it also avoids the negative condition or glitch from a Success as well. <br /> <br /> You can't detect any Aether without activating Aetheric Resonance, but you can still replenish Aether quite easily. Demons can recognize Infrastructure on sight, and can make the roll to gain Aether anytime an Angel nearby spends Essence, even if they don't know about the Angel. And a Demon can always go to Demonic Form, where it is impossible to be at 0 Aether because you gain Aether on assuming Demonic Form and gain Aether anytime you are at 0 in Demonic Form. <br /> <br /> It doesn't sound like any activity is required to learn Embeds and Exploits. Embeds are techniques they remember from their time as an Angel, they remember more of them as they get more powerful. Exploits are hacks that they piece together from Embeds they already know, since they all have Embed requirements they already have something the Demon has to do to learn them. Then they just spend the xp after some time thinking about the Embed to build the Exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T09:39:36-08:00","id":72033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hulsmanm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71231-assorted-dtd-rules-questions?p=71273#post71273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that Willpower can be spent on Compromise rolls. It can possibly be used to avoid compromises with Embeds, because some Embeds state that they cause Compromise on Success, but not on Exceptional Success. So you can't use it on the Compromise roll, but you can use it on the Embed roll to possibly avoid making a Compromise roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact in another thread someone's linked to a quote to one of the developers who seemed to confirm this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exceptional Success on a Compromise roll says that it gives a Cover Beat or regular Beat and a point of Willpower, I don't think it should grant a positive condition as well considering it also avoids the negative condition or glitch from a Success as well.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. That makes sense. I guess I still was not entirely clear on the relationship between exceptional successes and conditions as it seemed to be stated as universal rule in the GMC rules. Would you say the same is then true of the &quot;remove Glitch at the restoration facility&quot; roll?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't sound like any activity is required to learn Embeds and Exploits. Embeds are techniques they remember from their time as an Angel, they remember more of them as they get more powerful. Exploits are hacks that they piece together from Embeds they already know, since they all have Embed requirements they already have something the Demon has to do to learn them. Then they just spend the xp after some time thinking about the Embed to build the Exploit. </div> </div> </div>Ok, but that suggests to me that any cooperative ring would have identical Embeds as whenever one Demon discovers an Embed they can immediately teach it to the rest of the ring...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T19:40:40-08:00","id":74046,"title":"","content":"Speaking of rules... can I piggyback? I have a simple question.<br /> <br /> I was reading the section on demonic forms, and I have a question about Inhuman Reflexes. <br /> If it &quot;adds two dices to the rolls that uses dexterity [my paraphrase...]&quot; does it only add to active and contested rolls, or does the advantages such as Defense and Initiative change on the result of the activation of Inhuman Reflexes? You know, since, the latter are not actually rolls...<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T20:29:25-08:00","id":74071,"title":"","content":"By all means, let's have a consistent simple questions thread.<br /> <br /> And it does not add to defense or initiative, as of my understanding at this time. I'll have a look at it again though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T00:13:14-08:00","id":74148,"title":"","content":"Making sure I understand Occam's Razor correctly: Upon successfully activating the power, you gain up to [Primum] dots of &quot;buffer&quot; Cover, which are lost before your real Cover in the event of compromises generated by obvious supernatural manifestations and Exploits but not (barring an exceptional success on the Embed roll) on compromises owed to acting out of one's Cover, and (or?) the demon's compromise modifier from their Cover rating is adjusted to that of the higher rating in those situations.<br /> <br /> That about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T06:43:24-08:00","id":74238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71231-assorted-dtd-rules-questions?p=74071#post74071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means, let's have a consistent simple questions thread.<br /> <br /> And it does not add to defense or initiative, as of my understanding at this time. I'll have a look at it again though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was how I understood as well. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T22:22:45-08:00","id":74793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71231-assorted-dtd-rules-questions?p=74148#post74148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making sure I understand Occam's Razor correctly: Upon successfully activating the power, you gain up to [Primum] dots of &quot;buffer&quot; Cover, which are lost before your real Cover in the event of compromises generated by obvious supernatural manifestations and Exploits but not (barring an exceptional success on the Embed roll) on compromises owed to acting out of one's Cover, and (or?) the demon's compromise modifier from their Cover rating is adjusted to that of the higher rating in those situations.<br /> <br /> That about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my understanding of how this one works. The text would seem to imply that invoking a compromise for acting out of character doesn't gain any bonus from this embed unless you get an exceptional success, however.<br /> <br /> So, say we have a 5 Dot Cover, 3 Primum Demon and use this Embed.<br /> Normal Success we get the Supernatural Compromise at +2 (Effecive Rating 8) and Regular compromise at +0 (Effective Rating 5)<br /> Exceptional Success grants the Compromise at +2 (Effective Rating 8), regardless of situation.<br /> <br /> I'm just writing this for clarity, because the wording for this one is...tricky. It suggests that it provides the buffer for the whole scene, but only for supernatural manifestations. Using Occam's Razor (lol) seems to suggest that the bonus buffer is only for situations when it applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}